1
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:03,885
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,761 --> 00:00:06,137
Earth.

3
00:00:06,763 --> 00:00:08,097
Fire.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:10,141
Air.

5
00:00:11,184 --> 00:00:15,146
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,396 --> 00:00:18,608
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,651 --> 00:00:22,529
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,612 --> 00:00:23,821
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,905 --> 00:00:26,574
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:29,827
100 years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

11
00:00:29,911 --> 00:00:32,705
the new Avatar,
an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:32,956 --> 00:00:35,083
And although
his airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:37,752
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,835 --> 00:00:38,920
AANG: Oof.

15
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:42,090
KATARA: But I believe
Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:58,436 --> 00:01:02,648
( DRILL WHIRRING )

17
00:01:10,698 --> 00:01:12,325
( STEAM HISSING )

18
00:01:13,242 --> 00:01:15,286
( CREAKING )

19
00:01:32,887 --> 00:01:35,139
( WHIRRING )

20
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:47,068
This drill is a feat
of scientific ingenuity

21
00:01:47,151 --> 00:01:49,320
and raw destructive power.

22
00:01:49,737 --> 00:01:51,530
Once it tunnels
through the wall,

23
00:01:51,656 --> 00:01:53,866
our troops will
storm their city.

24
00:01:53,991 --> 00:01:56,285
The Earth Kingdom
will finally fall.

25
00:01:56,661 --> 00:02:00,206
And you can claim Ba Sing Se
in the name of your father.

26
00:02:00,748 --> 00:02:02,041
Nothing can stop us.

27
00:02:02,792 --> 00:02:06,212
Hmm, what about those
muscle-y guys down there?

28
00:02:08,798 --> 00:02:10,132
( DRILL WHIRRING )

29
00:02:10,216 --> 00:02:12,385
Please, the drill's metal shell

30
00:02:12,468 --> 00:02:15,012
is impervious to any
earthbending attack.

31
00:02:15,304 --> 00:02:17,974
Oh, I'm sure it is, War Minister Qin.

32
00:02:18,057 --> 00:02:19,642
But just to be
on the safe side,

33
00:02:19,934 --> 00:02:22,895
Mai and Ty Lee,
take the Earthbenders out.

34
00:02:22,979 --> 00:02:25,064
Finally, something to do.

35
00:02:30,778 --> 00:02:32,113
( MOMO CHATTERS )

36
00:02:32,488 --> 00:02:35,866
Aang, what are you doing here?
I thought you were looking for Appa.

37
00:02:35,950 --> 00:02:39,245
I was, but something
stopped me― Something big.

38
00:02:46,085 --> 00:02:48,337
SOKKA: Now, what's so big
that Appa has to wait?

39
00:02:49,338 --> 00:02:50,381
AANG: That.

40
00:02:51,007 --> 00:02:52,925
( DRILL WHIRRING )

41
00:02:54,385 --> 00:02:57,096
We made it to Ba Sing Se
and we're still not safe.

42
00:02:57,346 --> 00:02:58,431
No one is.

43
00:02:59,515 --> 00:03:01,100
What are you people doing here?

44
00:03:01,183 --> 00:03:02,977
Civilians aren't allowed on the wall.

45
00:03:03,602 --> 00:03:06,647
I'm the Avatar.
Take me to whoever's in charge.

46
00:03:07,982 --> 00:03:11,819
It is an honor to welcome you
to the Outer Wall, young Avatar.

47
00:03:12,403 --> 00:03:13,863
But your help is not needed.

48
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:17,325
- Not needed?
- Not needed.

49
00:03:17,616 --> 00:03:20,244
I have the situation
under control.

50
00:03:20,536 --> 00:03:24,248
I assure you, the Fire Nation
cannot penetrate this wall.

51
00:03:25,374 --> 00:03:29,420
Many have tried to break through it,
but none have succeeded.

52
00:03:30,421 --> 00:03:33,132
What about the Dragon of the West?
He got in.

53
00:03:33,215 --> 00:03:38,721
Well, technically, yes.
But he was quickly expunged.

54
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:44,143
Nevertheless, that's why the city
is named Ba Sing Se.

55
00:03:44,268 --> 00:03:46,937
It's the impenetrable city.

56
00:03:47,063 --> 00:03:49,398
They don't call it Na Sing Se!

57
00:03:49,482 --> 00:03:53,069
( LAUGHS ) That means penetrable city.

58
00:03:53,694 --> 00:03:54,945
Yeah, thanks for the tour.

59
00:03:55,029 --> 00:03:56,822
But we still got the drill problem.

60
00:03:57,239 --> 00:03:58,616
Not for long.

61
00:03:58,699 --> 00:04:01,952
To stop it, I've sent an elite
platoon of Earthbenders

62
00:04:02,036 --> 00:04:04,246
called the Terra Team.

63
00:04:04,330 --> 00:04:06,791
That's a good group name. Very catchy.

64
00:04:10,419 --> 00:04:11,420
( GRUNTING )

65
00:04:11,879 --> 00:04:13,339
( RUMBLING )

66
00:04:14,882 --> 00:04:17,510
Ready? Attack!

67
00:04:23,140 --> 00:04:24,600
( CREAKING )

68
00:04:26,852 --> 00:04:28,020
( GRUNTING )

69
00:04:36,779 --> 00:04:38,322
( GRUNTS )

70
00:04:40,116 --> 00:04:41,659
( GRUNTS )

71
00:04:44,829 --> 00:04:45,913
( GRUNTING )

72
00:04:47,164 --> 00:04:48,249
( GROANS )

73
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,293
We're doomed!

74
00:04:52,169 --> 00:04:54,088
Get a hold of yourself, man!

75
00:04:54,171 --> 00:04:55,631
You're right. I'm sorry.

76
00:04:56,132 --> 00:04:58,467
Maybe you'd like the Avatar's help now?

77
00:05:01,554 --> 00:05:02,721
( MEEKLY ) Yes, please.

78
00:05:05,641 --> 00:05:08,602
So the question is, how
are we gonna stop that thing?

79
00:05:10,729 --> 00:05:14,024
- Why are you all looking at me?
- You're the idea guy.

80
00:05:14,483 --> 00:05:17,069
So I'm the only one who
could ever come up with a plan?

81
00:05:17,153 --> 00:05:18,696
That's a lot of pressure.

82
00:05:18,779 --> 00:05:21,407
- And also, the complaining guy.
- That part I don't mind.

83
00:05:25,619 --> 00:05:30,249
So, Mr. Lee and Mister, um...
"Mushy," is it?

84
00:05:30,583 --> 00:05:31,834
It's pronounced "Moo-shi."

85
00:05:32,835 --> 00:05:34,753
You telling me how to do my job?

86
00:05:34,837 --> 00:05:36,881
Uh, no, no, no.

87
00:05:36,964 --> 00:05:40,134
But may I just say,
you're like a flower in bloom.

88
00:05:40,217 --> 00:05:43,012
Your beauty's intoxicating.

89
00:05:43,721 --> 00:05:47,057
Mmm, you're pretty easy on
the eyes yourself, handsome.

90
00:05:47,141 --> 00:05:48,392
Rawr!

91
00:05:48,809 --> 00:05:50,352
Welcome to Ba Sing Se.

92
00:05:53,772 --> 00:05:55,483
I'm gonna forget I saw that.

93
00:05:59,236 --> 00:06:01,572
I think Lee would make
a good Freedom Fighter.

94
00:06:01,947 --> 00:06:04,742
He's just trying to find his
way in the world, like us.

95
00:06:04,825 --> 00:06:07,036
You don't know
anything about him, Jet.

96
00:06:07,119 --> 00:06:09,497
I know he didn't get that
scar from a Waterbender.

97
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,916
Besides, I thought we
were going straight now.

98
00:06:11,999 --> 00:06:15,544
We are. And the new Freedom Fighters
could use a guy like Lee.

99
00:06:15,628 --> 00:06:16,962
What do you think, Longshot?

100
00:06:19,548 --> 00:06:20,883
I can respect that.

101
00:06:23,219 --> 00:06:25,804
What's wrong with him?
He doesn't look injured.

102
00:06:25,888 --> 00:06:27,097
His qi is blocked.

103
00:06:28,807 --> 00:06:32,144
- Who did this to you?
- Two girls ambushed us.

104
00:06:32,561 --> 00:06:35,064
One of them hit me with
a bunch of quick jabs.

105
00:06:35,147 --> 00:06:36,899
And suddenly, I couldn't earthbend,

106
00:06:36,982 --> 00:06:40,194
and I could barely move.
And then she cartwheeled away.

107
00:06:41,362 --> 00:06:43,656
Ty Lee. She doesn't look dangerous,

108
00:06:43,739 --> 00:06:46,242
but she knows the human body
and its weak points.

109
00:06:46,325 --> 00:06:48,869
It's like she takes you down
from the inside.

110
00:06:49,078 --> 00:06:51,580
- Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!
- Yes?

111
00:06:51,664 --> 00:06:52,790
What you just said.

112
00:06:52,873 --> 00:06:54,959
That's how we're gonna
take down the drill―

113
00:06:55,042 --> 00:06:57,711
The same way Ty Lee took
down all these big Earthbenders.

114
00:06:57,795 --> 00:06:59,630
By hitting its pressure points!

115
00:07:01,966 --> 00:07:03,968
We'll take it down from the inside.

116
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:11,809
( DRILL WHIRRING )

117
00:07:12,434 --> 00:07:15,312
Once I whip up some cover,
you're not gonna be able to see,

118
00:07:15,396 --> 00:07:16,689
so stay close to me.

119
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:20,234
( RUMBLING )

120
00:07:25,155 --> 00:07:26,407
TOPH: Run!

121
00:07:26,532 --> 00:07:27,575
( MOMO CHATTERS )

122
00:07:29,076 --> 00:07:31,412
Hey, look at that dust cloud.

123
00:07:31,537 --> 00:07:35,374
It's so... Poofy. Poof!

124
00:07:36,166 --> 00:07:38,836
Don't worry, Princess.
I'm sure it's nothing.

125
00:07:40,504 --> 00:07:41,922
( DRILL WHIRRING )

126
00:07:47,678 --> 00:07:49,722
( RUMBLING )

127
00:07:49,847 --> 00:07:51,181
Everyone into the hole.

128
00:07:55,603 --> 00:07:58,272
SOKKA: It's so dark down here.
I can't see a thing.

129
00:07:58,355 --> 00:08:00,691
TOPH: ( SARCASTICALLY )
Oh, no, what a nightmare!

130
00:08:00,816 --> 00:08:01,900
SOKKA: Sorry.

131
00:08:02,026 --> 00:08:04,612
( DRILL WHIRRING )

132
00:08:07,448 --> 00:08:08,741
There.

133
00:08:08,824 --> 00:08:09,825
( MOMO CHATTERS )

134
00:08:10,909 --> 00:08:11,910
( GRUNTS )

135
00:08:12,953 --> 00:08:13,954
( GRUNTS )

136
00:08:16,081 --> 00:08:17,291
Toph, come on!

137
00:08:17,416 --> 00:08:19,376
No way am I going in that metal monster.

138
00:08:19,501 --> 00:08:20,753
I can't bend in there.

139
00:08:20,878 --> 00:08:22,630
I'll try to slow it down out here.

140
00:08:22,755 --> 00:08:24,298
Okay, good luck.

141
00:08:26,342 --> 00:08:27,551
( RUMBLING )

142
00:08:28,177 --> 00:08:30,137
( GRUNTS )

143
00:08:33,974 --> 00:08:36,143
I need a plan of this machine,
some schematics

144
00:08:36,226 --> 00:08:38,020
that show what the inside looks like.

145
00:08:38,103 --> 00:08:39,730
Then we can find
its weak points.

146
00:08:39,813 --> 00:08:41,857
Where are we gonna
get something like that?

147
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:42,983
( CLANG )

148
00:08:43,067 --> 00:08:45,486
What are you doing?
Someone's gonna hear us.

149
00:08:45,694 --> 00:08:46,820
That's the point.

150
00:08:46,904 --> 00:08:49,782
I figure a machine this big
needs engineers to run it.

151
00:08:49,865 --> 00:08:52,701
- And when something breaks...
- They come to fix it.

152
00:08:52,785 --> 00:08:53,786
( GAS HISSING )

153
00:08:59,792 --> 00:09:00,793
Hi.

154
00:09:02,461 --> 00:09:03,962
This'll work, thanks!

155
00:09:04,588 --> 00:09:05,589
( CLANGS )

156
00:09:09,885 --> 00:09:12,638
It looks like the drill
is made up of two main structures.

157
00:09:12,721 --> 00:09:15,891
There's the inner mechanism,
where we are now, and the outer shell.

158
00:09:15,974 --> 00:09:18,977
The inner part and the outer part
are connected by these braces.

159
00:09:19,061 --> 00:09:21,689
If we cut through them, the
entire thing will collapse.

160
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:29,029
So, you guys got plans
once you're inside the city?

161
00:09:29,113 --> 00:09:32,741
MAN: Get your hot tea here!
Finest tea in Ba Sing Se!

162
00:09:33,158 --> 00:09:35,202
Oh, Jasmine, please!

163
00:09:40,374 --> 00:09:42,751
( COUGHS )

164
00:09:43,419 --> 00:09:46,338
Coldest tea in Ba Sing Se
is more like it.

165
00:09:46,463 --> 00:09:48,257
What a disgrace!

166
00:09:48,382 --> 00:09:50,134
Hey, can I talk to you for a second?

167
00:09:52,219 --> 00:09:53,804
( SIGHS )

168
00:09:53,929 --> 00:09:56,807
You and I have a much better
chance of making it in the city

169
00:09:56,890 --> 00:09:58,225
if we stick together.

170
00:09:58,350 --> 00:10:00,561
You wanna join the Freedom Fighters?

171
00:10:00,686 --> 00:10:03,564
Thanks, but I don't think
you want me in your gang.

172
00:10:03,647 --> 00:10:06,400
Come on, we made a great team
looting that captain's food.

173
00:10:06,483 --> 00:10:08,986
Think of all the good we
could do for these refugees.

174
00:10:09,069 --> 00:10:10,154
I said no.

175
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:12,364
Have it your way.

176
00:10:13,282 --> 00:10:14,783
( SLURPS )

177
00:10:23,584 --> 00:10:24,626
Hey!

178
00:10:24,710 --> 00:10:27,004
What are you doing firebending your tea?

179
00:10:27,087 --> 00:10:30,090
For a wise old man, that
was a pretty stupid move.

180
00:10:30,174 --> 00:10:33,677
I know you're not supposed
to cry over spilled tea, but...

181
00:10:33,761 --> 00:10:37,723
-( SNIFFLES ) It's just so sad!
-( TRAGIC VIOLIN PLAYS )

182
00:10:37,973 --> 00:10:40,601
( DRILL WHIRRING )

183
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:44,855
Wow, it looks a lot thicker in person
than it does in the plans.

184
00:10:44,938 --> 00:10:47,608
We're gonna have to work pretty
hard to cut through that.

185
00:10:47,691 --> 00:10:49,151
What's this "we" stuff?

186
00:10:49,234 --> 00:10:51,361
Aang and I are gonna
have to do all the work.

187
00:10:51,445 --> 00:10:53,197
Look, I'm the plan guy.

188
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:55,824
You two are the cut stuff
up with waterbending guys.

189
00:10:55,908 --> 00:10:57,951
Together, we're Team Avatar.

190
00:11:00,412 --> 00:11:05,584
( METAL SLICING )

191
00:11:13,926 --> 00:11:15,636
( PANTING )

192
00:11:15,719 --> 00:11:17,304
Come on, team! Don't quit now!

193
00:11:17,387 --> 00:11:19,139
- We're―
-( GROWLS )

194
00:11:19,223 --> 00:11:21,600
I mean, you're almost there!

195
00:11:23,227 --> 00:11:27,815
( METAL SLICING )

196
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:28,941
( MOMO CHATTERS )

197
00:11:30,859 --> 00:11:32,236
( CREAKING )

198
00:11:34,822 --> 00:11:36,156
( SIGHS )

199
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:39,743
At this rate, we won't do enough damage
before the drill reaches the wall.

200
00:11:39,827 --> 00:11:42,871
I don't know how many
more of those I have in me.

201
00:11:43,288 --> 00:11:45,040
( CREAKING )

202
00:11:45,123 --> 00:11:47,584
( RUMBLING )

203
00:11:48,252 --> 00:11:50,629
Do you hear that? We took it down!

204
00:11:50,712 --> 00:11:52,339
We better get out of here fast.

205
00:11:54,299 --> 00:11:56,385
QIN ( ON PA ):
Congratulations, crew!

206
00:11:56,510 --> 00:11:59,847
The drill has made contact
with the wall of Ba Sing Se.

207
00:11:59,972 --> 00:12:02,558
Start the countdown to victory!

208
00:12:02,683 --> 00:12:06,937
( CREW CHEERING )

209
00:12:09,565 --> 00:12:11,066
( DRILL WHIRRING )

210
00:12:20,284 --> 00:12:21,618
( DRILL WHIRRING )

211
00:12:29,376 --> 00:12:30,627
( GRUNTS )

212
00:12:30,711 --> 00:12:32,671
Come on, brace! Budge!

213
00:12:34,131 --> 00:12:36,800
( GRUNTS )

214
00:12:37,092 --> 00:12:39,428
This is bad. Really bad.

215
00:12:40,012 --> 00:12:43,348
( PANTING ) We're putting everything
we've got into busting these braces,

216
00:12:43,432 --> 00:12:44,683
but it's taking too long!

217
00:12:46,059 --> 00:12:48,270
Maybe we don't need to
cut all the way through.

218
00:12:48,729 --> 00:12:49,938
Toph has been teaching me

219
00:12:50,022 --> 00:12:53,400
that you shouldn't give 100%
of your energy into any one strike.

220
00:12:53,692 --> 00:12:55,611
Sokka, take a fighting stance.

221
00:12:55,694 --> 00:12:58,113
You've gotta be quick and accurate.

222
00:12:58,196 --> 00:13:01,450
Hit a series of points
and break your opponent's stance.

223
00:13:01,533 --> 00:13:04,703
And when he's reeling back,
you deliver the final blow.

224
00:13:04,786 --> 00:13:07,372
His own weight becomes
his downfall, literally.

225
00:13:08,123 --> 00:13:12,002
So we just need to weaken the braces
instead of cutting all the way through.

226
00:13:12,085 --> 00:13:13,879
Then I'll go to the top of this thing

227
00:13:13,962 --> 00:13:15,380
and deliver the final blow.

228
00:13:15,464 --> 00:13:18,091
And boom, it all comes crashing down!

229
00:13:18,342 --> 00:13:23,639
Everyone inside that wall,
the whole world, is counting on us.

230
00:13:23,722 --> 00:13:25,933
The whole world minus
the Fire Nation, that is.

231
00:13:27,851 --> 00:13:29,394
( GRUNTS )

232
00:13:29,478 --> 00:13:32,814
Come on, Twinkle Toes! Hurry up!

233
00:13:33,857 --> 00:13:39,696
( METAL SLICING )

234
00:13:45,702 --> 00:13:47,871
That's enough!
We need to get to the next one.

235
00:13:55,087 --> 00:13:57,547
MAN ( ON PA ): War Minister!
An engineer was ambushed.

236
00:13:57,631 --> 00:13:59,257
His schematics were stolen.

237
00:13:59,341 --> 00:14:00,592
MAN ( ON PA ): War Minister!

238
00:14:00,676 --> 00:14:03,345
A brace on the starboard side
has been cut clean through!

239
00:14:03,428 --> 00:14:04,805
It's sabotage, sir!

240
00:14:06,348 --> 00:14:07,557
Let's go, ladies.

241
00:14:09,226 --> 00:14:10,560
-( SPLASHING )
-( METAL SLICING )

242
00:14:10,644 --> 00:14:12,062
Good work, Team Avatar.

243
00:14:12,145 --> 00:14:14,231
Now Aang just needs to― Duck!

244
00:14:16,233 --> 00:14:17,234
Whoa!

245
00:14:17,943 --> 00:14:21,363
Wow, Azula, you were right!
It is the Avatar...

246
00:14:21,655 --> 00:14:22,948
...and friends.

247
00:14:23,949 --> 00:14:24,950
Hey.

248
00:14:25,867 --> 00:14:26,868
Aah!

249
00:14:29,454 --> 00:14:30,455
Whoa!

250
00:14:32,165 --> 00:14:33,250
( MOMO CHATTERS )

251
00:14:35,419 --> 00:14:38,255
Guys, get out of here!
I know what I need to do.

252
00:14:38,338 --> 00:14:40,716
Wait, you need this water
more than I do.

253
00:14:47,055 --> 00:14:48,807
Follow them. The Avatar's mine.

254
00:14:53,270 --> 00:14:54,646
Slurry pipeline?

255
00:14:54,730 --> 00:14:56,189
-( GRUNTS )
- What does that mean?

256
00:14:56,273 --> 00:14:57,691
( GRUNTS )

257
00:14:58,900 --> 00:15:00,569
It's rock and water mixed together.

258
00:15:00,652 --> 00:15:02,070
It means our way out.

259
00:15:04,197 --> 00:15:05,907
-( PANTING )
-( SPLASHES )

260
00:15:07,617 --> 00:15:08,827
( SCREAMING )

261
00:15:10,787 --> 00:15:13,206
Ugh, disgusting.

262
00:15:13,290 --> 00:15:16,710
Come on, you heard Azula.
We have to follow them.

263
00:15:16,793 --> 00:15:19,212
She can shoot all the
lightning she wants at me.

264
00:15:19,296 --> 00:15:22,132
I am not going in that
wall sludge juice.

265
00:15:22,215 --> 00:15:23,300
( SIGHS )

266
00:15:25,552 --> 00:15:26,803
( SPLASHES )

267
00:15:27,262 --> 00:15:28,263
Ugh.

268
00:15:39,483 --> 00:15:42,402
( SOKKA AND KATARA SCREAMING )

269
00:15:44,821 --> 00:15:45,822
Ugh!

270
00:15:45,906 --> 00:15:50,035
( GROANS AND WHINES )

271
00:15:50,118 --> 00:15:51,328
( MOANS )

272
00:15:57,042 --> 00:15:58,710
( SCREAMS )

273
00:16:00,045 --> 00:16:01,338
( WHIMPERS )

274
00:16:01,421 --> 00:16:04,549
Why don't you try blocking
my qi now, circus freak?

275
00:16:04,633 --> 00:16:06,051
Katara, keep that up.

276
00:16:06,134 --> 00:16:08,011
The pressure will
build up in the drill.

277
00:16:08,095 --> 00:16:11,139
Then, when Aang delivers the final blow,
it'll be ready to pop!

278
00:16:11,223 --> 00:16:12,682
( RUMBLING )

279
00:16:14,142 --> 00:16:17,062
( MOMO CHATTERS )

280
00:16:19,773 --> 00:16:21,566
This looks like a good spot, Momo.

281
00:16:22,442 --> 00:16:23,944
( EXCLAIMS )

282
00:16:27,239 --> 00:16:31,660
General Sung, tell your soldiers
to stop shooting rocks down here!

283
00:16:32,285 --> 00:16:33,912
Soldiers, whatever you do,

284
00:16:33,995 --> 00:16:36,123
don't stop shooting rocks down there!

285
00:16:39,793 --> 00:16:42,087
( CRASHING )

286
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:45,048
( METAL SLICING )

287
00:16:51,263 --> 00:16:54,349
Good technique, Little Sister.
Keep it up!

288
00:16:54,432 --> 00:16:56,059
Don't forget to breathe.

289
00:16:56,143 --> 00:17:00,063
You know, I am just about sick and tired
of you telling me what to do all day.

290
00:17:00,147 --> 00:17:01,940
You're like a chattering hog monkey.

291
00:17:02,023 --> 00:17:03,775
Just bend the slurry, woman!

292
00:17:04,401 --> 00:17:06,486
-( SCREAMS )
- TOPH: You guys need some help?

293
00:17:06,570 --> 00:17:08,530
Toph, help me plug up this drain.

294
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:16,663
( CREAKING )

295
00:17:19,624 --> 00:17:22,127
( METAL SLICING )

296
00:17:23,211 --> 00:17:24,588
( PANTING )

297
00:17:24,671 --> 00:17:26,423
What I'd give
to be a Metalbender.

298
00:17:26,506 --> 00:17:27,632
( SQUEALS )

299
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:32,304
- Momo, get out of here!
-( CHATTERS )

300
00:17:47,027 --> 00:17:48,570
( WATER SPLASHING )

301
00:17:57,746 --> 00:17:59,831
- Aah!
-( CRASHING )

302
00:18:04,336 --> 00:18:05,337
( GASPS )

303
00:18:11,301 --> 00:18:13,970
( GRUNTS )

304
00:18:15,931 --> 00:18:16,932
( GRUNTS )

305
00:18:21,478 --> 00:18:22,520
( GRUNTS )

306
00:18:28,735 --> 00:18:29,736
( GRUNTS )

307
00:18:30,362 --> 00:18:31,821
( GAS HISSING )

308
00:18:32,864 --> 00:18:34,241
( CREAKING )

309
00:18:35,533 --> 00:18:37,827
( RUMBLING )

310
00:18:48,088 --> 00:18:49,923
( WHIMPERS )

311
00:18:56,263 --> 00:18:57,347
( GRUNTS )

312
00:19:07,524 --> 00:19:08,525
Whoa!

313
00:19:13,571 --> 00:19:14,572
Aah!

314
00:19:17,075 --> 00:19:18,243
( GRUNTS )

315
00:19:31,047 --> 00:19:33,717
-( CHATTERS )
-( GRUNTS )

316
00:19:39,014 --> 00:19:40,932
Thanks, Momo. I owe you one.

317
00:19:46,313 --> 00:19:48,481
- Now all I need is a―
-( CRASHES )

318
00:19:48,565 --> 00:19:50,567
Actually, that is what I needed, for once.

319
00:19:50,650 --> 00:19:51,776
( MOMO CHATTERS )

320
00:19:54,529 --> 00:19:57,615
( STONE CRACKING )

321
00:20:17,427 --> 00:20:19,179
Aah!

322
00:20:31,358 --> 00:20:32,359
Aah!

323
00:20:36,154 --> 00:20:37,405
Aah!

324
00:20:38,615 --> 00:20:39,783
( CREAKING )

325
00:20:40,784 --> 00:20:42,077
( CREAKING )

326
00:20:46,498 --> 00:20:49,626
( SPLASHING )

327
00:20:49,709 --> 00:20:51,252
- Woo-hoo!
- Here it comes!

328
00:20:56,424 --> 00:20:57,425
Whoa!

329
00:21:03,681 --> 00:21:05,308
( CREAKING )

330
00:21:08,978 --> 00:21:11,147
( DRILL POWERS DOWN )

331
00:21:19,030 --> 00:21:20,323
( CHATTERS )

332
00:21:34,254 --> 00:21:36,005
( SPUTTERS ) Ugh!

333
00:21:44,097 --> 00:21:45,306
We lost.

334
00:21:46,766 --> 00:21:49,185
MAN: Last call for Ba Sing Se!

335
00:21:49,561 --> 00:21:51,312
Jet, relax.

336
00:21:51,396 --> 00:21:53,982
So the old guy had some hot tea. Big deal!

337
00:21:54,065 --> 00:21:58,236
He heated it himself.
Those guys are Firebenders.

338
00:22:09,414 --> 00:22:12,834
- What a handsome baby.
- Thank you.

339
00:22:33,521 --> 00:22:36,774
SOKKA: I just wanted to say
good effort out there today, Team Avatar.

340
00:22:36,858 --> 00:22:39,360
Enough with the Team Avatar stuff.

341
00:22:39,444 --> 00:22:42,322
No matter how many times you
say it, it's not gonna catch on.

342
00:22:42,405 --> 00:22:45,575
How about the Boomerang Squad?

343
00:22:45,658 --> 00:22:47,660
See, it's good 'cause
it's got "ang" in it.

344
00:22:47,744 --> 00:22:49,370
Boomer-Aang!

345
00:22:49,454 --> 00:22:50,788
I kinda like that one.

346
00:22:50,872 --> 00:22:53,249
Let's talk about this
on our way into the city.

347
00:22:53,333 --> 00:22:55,376
- The Aang Gang?
- KATARA: Sokka...

348
00:22:55,460 --> 00:22:57,795
- The Fearsome Foursome!
- TOPH: You're crazy.

349
00:22:57,879 --> 00:22:59,255
Why? We're fearsome!
